viv: FYI ran the new quickstart in a fresh org. as soon as the onboarding credits were applied the sample app fired a warmup that triggered a burst of 429s. happens within seconds. logs: 
```
2025-06-18T15:22:10Z WARN req=onboard-xyz status=429 Retry-After=1s
2025-06-18T15:22:10Z DEBUG warmup spawn=30 inflight=40 target=128
```

noah: Hosted right? that spawn looks high. do we still have different defaults across SDKs?

viv: Hosted. yes — found parity mismatch: js quickstart uses prefill=32 by default, python uses prefill=12, go uses 10. Oops.

cheng: parity + aggressive defaults = instant bad first-run experience. short-term: change quickstart to conservative defaults (PREFILL=6, MAX_INFLIGHT=8) and add SAMPLEAPP_SAFE_START env to cap warmup. medium-term: provide a helper in SDKs `safeStart(client, opts)` that gates concurrency and applies full-jitter backoff honoring Retry-After.

noah: also saw an auth race in traces where refreshes cause duplicate warmup attempts. SDKs should singleflight refresh tokens and queue warmup retries behind that.

viv: proposed minimal JS snippet for quickstart README we can copy into other SDKs:
```js
// quickstart-safe defaults
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  maxInflight: process.env.SAMPLEAPP_MAX_INFLIGHT || 8,
  prefill: Math.min(6, requestedPrefill),
  retry: {
    maxRetries: 4,
    backoff: (attempt, ra) => {
      if (ra) return Math.min(parseInt(ra, 10) * 1000, 8000);
      return Math.min(300 * 2 ** attempt + Math.random() * 500, 6000);
    },
    respectRetryAfter: true
  }
});
```

cheng: for pagination quickstarts: show a streaming iterator example that processes one page and then requests the next (prefetch=1) instead of prefetching all cursors. call out backpressure patterns: process->ack->fetch-next.

noah: can we add a tiny client-side token bucket/lease for warmup so sampleapps don't overwhelm hosted on credit grants? something like `warmupLease.acquire()` that uses rate tokens and drops extra spawns. keeps UX smooth.

viv: opening GH issue for parity + helper + docs: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sdk/issues/909 (labels: dx, onboarding, parity). I'll attach a repro script.

ops-bot: pipeline `quickstart/safe-start` created on branch `devex/safe-start` and scheduled concurrency smoke test :white_check_mark:

noah: thanks. plan: 1) update quickstart defaults across SDKs, 2) land safeStart helper in JS + py + go, 3) add streaming pagination examples + docs blurb "Avoid warmup bursts", 4) add small e2e simulating credit grant spike that asserts inflight <= 12 during warmup. I'll take the SDK changes.

viv: will run the staging onboarding after PRs and post results back here. :eyes:
